# The keys a release of Collectu Core is signed with, in the allowed signers format of ssh-keygen(1).
#
# A Core updates only to a release whose tag carries a valid signature of one of these keys
# (src/utils/signed_releases.py). The first release ahead of it is checked against this file as the
# Core already runs it - never as the release itself ships it - and each release that passes hands
# its own copy on to the next (src/utils/updater.py). So a release cannot vouch for itself: a new
# key is trusted only from a release signed with a key that was trusted before it. The release
# workflow refuses to tag with a key that is not listed here.
#
# Only ed25519 keys are accepted. One line per key:
#
#   release@collectu.de namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...
#
# Keep a second, offline recovery key here as well - without one, a lost release key means updating
# every Core by hand. Rotating the key, and what to do when it is lost or leaked: "Release key
# handling" in SECURITY.md.
release@collectu.de namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIDK7FQ/onXpU/74Ga468WGZBfaKkrAN4h9ppdD0x2PKV collectu-core release recovery
release@collectu.de namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAINDhqLKhlwHQbHOtJ6vG7sNvROBho17KDMMJM8OmJOV4 collectu-core release signing
